+The order $(2,0,0)$ used in the substitution checks was fixed a priori. To
+document how a standard procedure would behave on the same data, we ran
+\texttt{auto\_arima} (AIC, $d=0$, $p,q\le5$, with constant) on the $h=1$
+training window of 20 evenly spaced evaluated origins per domain (windows of
+216--720 observations), using the windows of the rolling-origin protocol.
+No refitting of the reported check was performed with these orders.
